all_candidate_instructions.dataflow_inspector:
Carefully trace the code script from line 1 to identify every line that touches the target column: where it is read, referenced (by name or subscript, e.g. df['col'], row['col']), written, filtered, transformed, aggregated, merged, or selected for output.

Count line numbers accurately starting from line 1 at the very first line of the script. Double-check that each identified line or range actually contains an explicit reference to the target column or directly operates on it. Put adjacent lines in one range.

Output only JSON: { "sources": [{ "start_line": int, "end_line": int }, ...] }
